    "_comment": "GROK · TableFrame.grok used the way you would use it in your own project: called inline in a regular @transformer body, with the parsed result feeding ordinary filter/select/with_columns/join/sort work and landing as parquet. Covers the basic line split, a numeric capture plus a second grok over the log's file name, and a join between two separately parsed logs. Each example is a pub->tfr->sub chain over gk_logs (LocalFileSrc with SrcFileFormat.LOG, reading one staged world CSV as LINES: columns `file` + `message`) / gk_marts (@transformer, calls TableFrame.grok inline and then does ordinary filter/select/join/sort work on the result) / gk_out (LocalFileDest, writes each mart as parquet). They assert nothing — they are meant to be READ, and each file also runs standalone (`python functions/gk_ex_<name>.py`). Generated by gen_suites.py."
